--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
WHAT SHIPPED
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
A complete, HIG-native SwiftUI DriveScorePage at web parity: a pure @Observable state holder
(ADR-004 — no networking in the view) over an injectable DriveScoreDataSource seam whose methods
keep the web hook names at the Swift call sites (useDriveScore ← GET /drives/score, useDrives ←
GET /drives?vehicle_id, loadVehicles ← useSelectedVehicle/GET /vehicles). The web client-side
scoring algorithm (scoreDrive: 40 pt efficiency from derived Wh/km, 30 pt smoothness from average
power, 30 pt speed-discipline above 90 mph) and every aggregation (avgScores, trendChartData,
categoryBarData, histogramData, periodStats, best/worst, weakestCategory, achievements, tips) are
ported verbatim into the deterministic, unit-tested DriveScoreEngine.

The page reproduces the web chrome (PageContainer title + subtitle + the global VehicleSelect +
the RangePicker date filter) and ALL of the web's StaggerItem sections:

  Hero overall-score gauge (GlassPanel1 + RadialGauge tinted by grade), the grade badge (GlassPanel2),
  the three category gauges (GlassPanel3/4/5 + RadialGauge + MetricBar + InlineMetric), the
  score-trend line chart (GlassPanel6 + Score-Trend ChartContainer + LineChart + 80-pt A reference),
  the category-breakdown bars (GlassPanel8 + Category-Breakdown ChartContainer + BarChart), the
  score-distribution histogram (GlassPanel10 + Score-Distribution ChartContainer + BarChart), the
  improvement tips (GlassPanel12), the best/worst drive cards (GlassPanel13/14 + RadialGauge), the
  sortable + paginated drive-history table (GlassPanel15), the four summary stat cards (Avg-Score /
  Best-Score / Total-Drives / Avg-Efficiency), the six weekly/monthly period-stat cards
  (GlassPanel20-25) with the noPeriodStats empty (GlassPanel26), the achievement badges
  (GlassPanel27), and the two breakdown KVLists (Card28 Score Breakdown + Card29 Period Statistics).

All measurements stay SI canonical in the model (meters / seconds / m·s⁻¹ / Wh / W); conversion to
the user's unit preference happens ONLY at the SwiftUI render boundary via the shared KMP Units
facade + DriveScoreFormat (ADR-005). Adaptive across macOS/iPad regular width vs. iPhone compact
(ADR-002/006): the gauge grid, the best/worst row, the period-stat grid, the achievement grid, and
the KVLists reflow; the history grid scrolls horizontally on compact. Every visible literal resolves
from Localizable.xcstrings with the web key names (zero hardcoded text). Navigation: registered for
the .driving route (DriveScoreRouteRegistration), reachable + deep-linkable via the new
AppRouteParser alias "/drive-score" → .driving (mirrors the sibling "/statistics" → .analytics).

There is no map (manifest declares 0 maps). The data sources are not live SSE streams (drives +
score are request/response), so no staleness indicator applies.

